# Data and auth

Marketing phase plus the seeker Places feed and staff portal. Do not add matcher scoring tables beyond `listing_embeddings` / `seeker_needs`. Calendar and document parser wait until asked.

## Layout

- `supabase/migrations/20260918000000_listings.sql`: canonical schema + sample sites. Same contents as `supabase/seed.sql`.
- `lib/listings/types.ts`: enums. Never free-text categories.
- `lib/listings/queries.ts`: server fetch of featured and published listings. Falls back to `lib/listings/seed.ts` if the table is missing. Keep seed IDs in lockstep with the SQL.
- `app/(app)/places`: seeker feed and `/places/[id]` detail pages. Testers are the sample sites. Staff publish more from `/portal`.
- `lib/matching/rank.ts`: calls `match_listings` when a seeker embedding exists. Otherwise keeps `sort_order`.
- `lib/matching/hard-filters.ts`: pets, couples, vehicle, full lot. Removes a listing. Does not score.
- `lib/supabase/client.ts`: browser client. Returns `null` when env is missing.
- `lib/supabase/server.ts`: cookie session for Route Handlers.
- `proxy.ts`: Next.js 16 session refresh (this is middleware).
- `app/auth/callback/route.ts`: PKCE code exchange for Google and magic links.
- `components/auth/sign-in-dialog.tsx`: password, magic link, Google.
- `scripts/run-sql.mjs`: `npm run db:setup`. Prefers `npx supabase db query --linked --project-ref` after `npx supabase login`. Applies listings, provider portal, and vector search migrations.

## Tables

One listing row per **physical site**, linked to an organization.

- `organizations`: `id`, `name`, `description`, `access_code`
- `listings`: `kind` `shelter` | `parking`; `freshness` `live` | `recent` | `call_first`; `pets` / `couples` enums or null; parking uses `parking_status` `open` | `full` | `waitlist` plus `vehicle_note`. `lat` / `lng` for near-me distance. `phone` for call intake. `intake_method` `call` | `waitlist` | `register` | `walk_up`. `featured` + `sort_order` drive the homepage hero (first three). `published` puts a row on `/places`.
- `listing_interest`: seeker waitlist / register / on-the-way rows. Not matcher scoring. Own-row write. Org staff can read.
- Places feed day-of filters (distance, intake, freshness, hide full lots) live in `lib/listings/place-filters.ts`. Hard filters still remove listings. Distance sorts client-side. It is not a second matcher.
- `profiles`: `id` = `auth.users.id`, `role` `seeker` | `provider`. Created by `handle_new_user` on signup.
- `organization_members`: staff roles for the portal.
- `listing_embeddings` / `seeker_needs`: vector ranking only. The Places feed calls `match_listings` when a row exists.

RLS: anon and authenticated **select** published listings and their orgs. Members can read drafts. Profiles are own-row only.

## Apply SQL

Anon key cannot create tables. After `npx supabase login`, run `npm run db:setup`. That uses `supabase db query --linked --project-ref`. Fallback: paste `supabase/seed.sql` into the SQL editor, or add `SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN`.

Project in `.env.local`: `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` / `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` only in client code. Never commit real keys.

## Auth

- Email/password and magic link write `role` into user metadata on create.
- Google: `signInWithOAuth({ provider: "google" })` → `/auth/callback`. Role is taken from the landing page (`/` seeker, `/for-providers` provider), not a dialog question. New accounts get that role; existing ones do not change.
- Dashboard: Site URL `http://localhost:3000`. Redirect URLs live in `supabase/config.toml` (`additional_redirect_urls`) and were pushed for local callbacks. Google provider still needs a Cloud client ID/secret in Auth > Providers. Google Cloud authorized redirect: `https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback`.
- If Google is not enabled, the button still shows; Supabase returns an error toast. Do not fake a session.

## Homepage listings

Hero reads `getFeaturedListings()` and slices the first three. Cards link to `/places/[id]`. The Places feed lists every published site. Do not add a second strip on the homepage that repeats those cards.
